            "review_text": "maloneranger60\nAlbany, New York127 contributions\n0\nLoud Live Music\nNov 2016 • Friends\nI know, I know...the older you are the louder it is. My wife and I and a couple of friends went into the Quarter Pub recently. Cool space. Nice crowd. Cold beer. Decent food. The live music started and it looked like it could be, well, amateur hour. At first, we all cringed as the music blasted away at our fillings. But then we realized, somewhere in the excessive volume was real talent. Sure, a little raw but actually quite good. A young woman took over lead singer duties soon after the opening set and she was even better. I don't want to ruin things for the kids, but take the volume down below 11 and you might have a real nice venue for up and coming local talent. As we walked out, we bumped into the young owner. Very nice guy. I hope he does well.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten December 6, 2016",
            "rating": 5.0,
